; chunkbatch.eval - a multi-square fill rebuilds each touched chunk ONCE, at
; the end, and still leaves no chunk stale (editor-updates P0).
;
; `geomlayout` (printed by geomhash) compares the chunks actually UPLOADED with
; what a fresh bake would upload; a chunk the batch forgot shows as STALE. Each
; fill is followed by one, and the fills cover the cases a batch has to get
; right: a recolour, a type change (floor raised to wall, which moves the wall
; faces of the NEIGHBOURING chunks too), a flood, and the undo of all of them.
; The fills are timed - the whole point of the batch.

logecho on
reset
geomhash
echo --- recolour a 10x8 block of floor ---
editor fill floors floor_slabs rect 3 3 12 10
geomhash
echo --- raise a 3x3 block to wall, straddling chunk edges ---
editor fill walls wall_brick_old rect 15 7 17 9
geomhash
echo --- flood the recoloured block (it is one texture now, so it floods) ---
editor fill floors floor_cobble_mossy flood 5 5
geomhash
echo --- undo all three (a rect is two steps: the corner click, then the fill) ---
; An undo DEFERS its rebake to editor close, so the layout reads "deferred"
; here by design; the surface hashes are what say the undo was complete.
undo
undo
undo
undo
undo
geomhash
